  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Yogesh vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 28 August, 2019 Author: Vandana Kasrekar Bench: Vandana Kasrekar The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh Crr-4240-2019 (Yogesh Vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh) Indore, Dated : 28-08-2019 Shri Dharmendra Chelawat, counsel for the petitioner. Shri Lokesh Mehta, Ga for the respondent / State.",
    "facts": "The petitioner has been convicted under section 16(1)(a) (i) and (ii) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 and sentenced to undergo six months R.I with fine of Rs. 1000/- on each count. It has been submitted on behalf of the petitioner submits that the petitioner has been falsely implicated in the present offence.",
    "arguments": "There is no possibility of final hearing of the revision at an early date. A bare perusal of the records, it reveals that the petitioner has fair chance of success in the revision. and therefore, he prays for grant of bail and suspension of jail sentence. Learned GA for the respondent / State opposes the application stating that no case is made out for suspension of jail sentence and grant of bail as there is ample evidence available on record against the present petitioner.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "There is no possibility of final hearing of the revision at an early date. A bare perusal of the records, it reveals that the petitioner has fair chance of success in the revision.",
    "respondent_arguments": "and therefore, he prays for grant of bail and suspension of jail sentence. Learned GA for the respondent / State opposes the application stating that no case is made out for suspension of jail sentence and grant of bail as there is ample evidence available on record against the present petitioner.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
